								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=902.msg8985#msg8985"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=902.msg8985#msg8985">Re: Person who made a big impact on your EQ life</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #3 on:</b> July 03, 2004, 12:07:42 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							OMG Kimmie......making me think! (shame on j00!!!)<br /><br />Well, let&#039;s see.....<br />Kimentari - got me started playing EQ after she told me &quot;EQ is so much better than UO, you just gotta try it!&quot;<br />Sindee - long-time-ago Shammy who gave me my first guild tag.......Shadows of Honor <br />Ciil - my first mentor as a druid. Was and still is on of my best friends in this alternate reality. Was (still is!) always there when I needed a helping hand. <br />Kumaddar, Yanke, Debonshire (Lindale), Lethial (Nynne) and Alcoll - The Crew! God we had some good times!!!!!
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
